+2 P.S., +2 P.E., +4 Spd, stored unconditionally. Considered supernatural beings: prose. || TATTOOS follow the catalog''s convention (stone-master): magic tattoos are prose special abilities, there being no tattoo catalog. The 15 starting picks are listed by category; Monster-Shaping is a costing system by M.D.C. tier and stays prose. || SKILLS: the book heads the list O.O.C. Skills (a typo for O.C.C.). Radio: Basic 45+10. Languages and Literacy Dragonese/Elf, American and Greek at 98%: Language: Dragonese and Literacy: Dragonese/Elven at 98; American as Language: Native Tongue and Literacy: Native Language at 98 (the catalog''s convention); Greek as Language: Ancient Greek 98 and a Literacy: Other pick at 98 (no Greek literacy row; a fixed Literacy: Other grant is refused by regression). Two languages of choice +15% as two Language: Other picks. Intelligence 32+15, Tracking is the catalog Tracking (people) 25+10, Wilderness Survival 30+15, Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+25, Lore: Magic 25+15, Disguise 25+15, Concealment 20+15. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts with no upgrade price printed, so no hand_to_hand block. || RELATED: four, plus three additional skills at levels four, eight and twelve, read as one at each of those levels (three in all); the alternative reading, three at each, is the one to revisit. Pilot except robot and power armor skills excludes Robots & Power Armor and every Robot Combat row. Rogue +4% is as printed. || COMPOSITION: taken with a race that states its own M.D.C., P.P.E. or Horror Factor (the Chiang-Ku), the race values win; the book does not say the class replaces the race, so no supersedes_race. || MONEY: the book prints none; starting_money omitted. || EQUIPMENT: a TW energy rifle and energy pistol, mapped to tw-converted-energy-rifle and tw-converted-energy-pistol; anything else suiting the mission, and a masquerading monster''s own armor and gear, is prose."
