## Lore

Clan Skellian, the Atlanteans who developed the Monster-Shaping tattoos, trained a special force of tattooed warriors modelled on the Undead Slayers of Rifts Atlantis. Monster Hunters are schooled in subterfuge and espionage and carry tattoos suited to the work. The most adept have slipped into the inhuman cities of Cibola, New Dragcona and Splynn on spying and rescue missions. Others wander as champions of justice, often passing as the inhuman sidekick or slave of a more human-looking companion (a True Atlantean, an Amazon or a warrior or spy) to explain their monstrous shape. Many young Skellian Atlanteans volunteer for the O.C.C. to prepare for adventuring abroad, and for most it is their first taste of combat.

Standard equipment is typically a TW energy rifle and energy pistol, plus whatever weapons and gear a mission calls for. When disguised as a monster, the Monster Hunter wears the armor and carries the equipment that creature would normally use.

## Magic Tattoos

Starting tattoos (15, besides the Marks of Heritage): one simple weapon, two magic weapons, two animals, two monsters, four Monster-Shaping, three powers, and one more of any category. The tattoos themselves are described in Rifts Atlantis. Each level adds two simple tattoos (animal or simple weapon) or one major one (powers, monster, Monster-Shaping or magic weapon), no more than two at a time and at least six months apart.

## Monster-Shaping Tattoos

A new category of tattoo magic known only to Clan Skellian and a few Chiang-Ku dragons, who helped the Skellian alchemists develop it. It does not transform the True Atlantean, who cannot be transformed, but surrounds him with an ectoplasm-like false body: in effect a magical monster costume or suit of armor with some illusion mixed in.

P.P.E. to activate, by the race imitated:

- Beings with less than 1000 S.D.C. and/or hit points: 30 P.P.E.
- M.D.C. races with less than 60 M.D.C.: 60 P.P.E.
- M.D.C. races with 61 to 200 M.D.C.: 90 P.P.E.
- M.D.C. races with 201 to 1000 M.D.C.: 120 P.P.E.
- M.D.C. races with 1001 to 3000 M.D.C.: 200 P.P.E. (the limit)

Duration is 30 minutes per level of experience. The false body''s M.D.C. can never exceed 800 or twice the character''s natural M.D.C., whichever is more, so an adult dragon''s shape gives at most 800 M.D.C. Ogres, trolls, wolfen, brodkil, gurgoyles, giants, dragons and sphinxes are ideal disguises; anything smaller than the wearer cannot be imitated. Other tattoos and magic can be used to simulate the abilities the false shape lacks.

## True Atlanteans

The racial block the book prints with this O.C.C., for a True Atlantean Monster Hunter (played with no R.C.C.):

- Alignment: any, most principled, scrupulous or unprincipled.
- Attributes: I.Q. 3D6+4, M.E. 4D6+6, M.A. 3D6+4, P.S. 4D6+4, P.P. 3D6, P.E. 3D6+6, P.B. 3D6+6, Spd 4D6+6.
- Hit Points: P.E. +1D6 per level. S.D.C.: 50 plus O.C.C., tattoo and physical skill S.D.C. Only Undead Slayers and Tattooed Men are mega-damage creatures.
- Horror Factor: 14 for an Undead Slayer, 12 for the average Atlantean.
- P.P.E. base 10, plus 12 from the Marks of Heritage and six per additional tattoo, plus any magic O.C.C.''s.
- Height 6 ft plus 1D4 inches, plus an inch per century of age; weight 170 lbs and up. Appear 19 to 35 while anywhere from 19 to 250 years old; the average life span is 500 years.
- Appearance entirely human: tall, handsome, dark-haired. Typically bold, headstrong loners, but kind, merciful, noble, honest and brave. Usually Hand to Hand: Expert or Martial Arts.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'atlantean-monster-hunter');


